<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I74e7eb01d27213b3be6d6b7a66c720b2bc2ed749" commit="222a5ac32640976561edbe55fb652c7a5637efec" commit_message="CRAS: Add first input timing test.  Simplest possible input timing test.  One device, one stream, one wake.  Change-Id: I74e7eb01d27213b3be6d6b7a66c720b2bc2ed749 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/586631 Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="586631" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/31/586631/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If60e433e281e2e43d94001605b8cd81de62fab1d" commit="5ec21f6101dd484d389760068b7fe4d8783f1573" commit_message="CRAS: timing_ut - Factor out common single-device tests  Having a helper function will make it easier to add tests with streams at different levels.  Change-Id: If60e433e281e2e43d94001605b8cd81de62fab1d Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/590713 Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="590713" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/13/590713/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I539ee2b9e6582d242b6d83f2a2541185cafe53ba" commit="f4de20d63bcaa6d5e4f23900b8f4aa91d37d2864" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Store a permanent error in obj-&gt;mm.pages  Once the object has been truncated, it is unrecoverable. To facilitate detection of this state store the error in obj-&gt;mm.pages.  This is required for the next patch which should be applied to v4.10 (via stable), so we also need to mark this patch for backporting. In that regard, let's consider this to be a fix/improvement too.  v2: Avoid dereferencing the ERR_PTR when freeing the object.  Fixes: 1233e2db199d (&quot;drm/i915: Move object backing storage manipulation to its own locking&quot;) Signed-off-by: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Cc: Joonas Lahtinen &lt;joonas.lahtinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Cc: &lt;stable@vger.kernel.org&gt; # v4.10+ Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20170307132031.32461-1 -chris@chris-wilson.co.uk Reviewed-by: Joonas Lahtinen &lt;joonas.lahtinen@linux.intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 4e5462ee843c883790e9609cf560d88960ea4227) Signed-off-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 0d9dc306e15b59bf50db87ebcb1e2248586d4733) Signed-off-by: Patrick Waterlander &lt;patrick.waterlander@intel.com&gt;  BUG=b:63740184 TEST=Build for poppy with USE=kasan and boot  Change-Id: I539ee2b9e6582d242b6d83f2a2541185cafe53ba Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/602573 Commit-Ready: Patrick Waterlander &lt;patrick.waterlander@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Casey G Bowman &lt;casey.g.bowman@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="602573" owner_email="patrick.waterlander@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/602573/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I48a7a25fd95d085d2f01b3aa7991c992cd38a574" commit="4589ef7468b86e741ac053b628697d2f46e24c53" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Use pagecache write to prepopulate shmemfs from pwrite-ioctl  Before we instantiate/pin the backing store for our use, we can prepopulate the shmemfs filp efficiently using a write into the pagecache. We avoid the penalty of instantiating all the pages, important if the user is just writing to a few and never uses the object on the GPU, and using a direct write into shmemfs allows it to avoid the cost of retrieving a page (mostly the clear-before-use, but in theory we could curtail swapin) before it is overwritten.  This can be extended later to provide additional specialisation for other backends (other than shmemfs). For now it provides a defense against very large write-only allocations from exhausting all of system memory.  v2: Smelling fixes.  Fixes: fe115628d567 (&quot;drm/i915: Implement pwrite without struct-mutex&quot;) References: https://bugs.freedesktop.org/show_bug.cgi?id=99107 Signed-off-by: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Cc: Matthew Auld &lt;matthew.william.auld@gmail.com&gt; Cc: Joonas Lahtinen &lt;joonas.lahtinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Cc: Mika Kuoppala &lt;mika.kuoppala@linux.intel.com&gt; Cc: &lt;stable@vger.kernel.org&gt; # v4.10+ Reviewed-by: Joonas Lahtinen &lt;joonas.lahtinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Tvrtko Ursulin &lt;tvrtko.ursulin@intel.com&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20170307120338.7277-2 -chris@chris-wilson.co.uk (cherry picked from commit 7c55e2c5772dcf3cbacd0fa2bcfeefae416b73f7) Signed-off-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 4e6fdafa7ac395ad47a80a0e7b4fd1e11550f862) Signed-off-by: Patrick Waterlander &lt;patrick.waterlander@intel.com&gt;  BUG=b:63740184 TEST=Build for poppy with USE=kasan and boot  Change-Id: I48a7a25fd95d085d2f01b3aa7991c992cd38a574 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/602574 Commit-Ready: Patrick Waterlander &lt;patrick.waterlander@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Casey G Bowman &lt;casey.g.bowman@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="602574" owner_email="patri